From: WhaleOS <whaleos-dev@navercorp.com>
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] config_base: drop CAP_WAKE_ALARM from the container

CAP_WAKE_ALARM in the container's bounding set lets any process inside
Waydroid create CLOCK_BOOTTIME_ALARM / CLOCK_REALTIME_ALARM timerfd
handles -- Android AlarmManager's wake-capable alarms.  Every armed
alarm of that kind is a registered kernel wakeup source; when the
timer fires the kernel calls __pm_stay_awake and the wake source stays
active until userspace reads the fd.

Combined with powerd's cgroup-freezer-based suspend, this races: if an
alarm fires while the container is frozen the holding thread is stuck
in __refrigerator() and cannot call __pm_relax, leaving pm_get_wakeup_count()
blocked forever (powerd wchan = pm_get).  Removing the cap forces
AlarmManager onto plain CLOCK_BOOTTIME which doesn't register a wake
source.

CAP_BLOCK_SUSPEND is left in the bounding set on purpose: Android's
InputManagerService (libinputreader EventHub) requires EPOLLWAKEUP on
its wake pipe and aborts with "Input must be able to block suspend to
properly process events" if it can't get one.  Dropping
CAP_BLOCK_SUSPEND would put system_server into a respawn loop and make
the entire Android container unusable.

The wake-source-leak risk that CAP_BLOCK_SUSPEND keeps open is mitigated
separately by a powerd suspend-delay client inside waydroid_helper that,
on every SuspendImminent, runs `cmd deviceidle force-idle deep` inside
the container to make Android release its non-critical wake locks
before powerd freezes the cgroup.  See platform2/waydroid_helper/.

Note: the original line listed `wake_alarm` twice (an upstream Waydroid
copy/paste); both occurrences are removed.

--- a/data/configs/config_base
+++ b/data/configs/config_base
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 lxc.autodev = 0
 # lxc.autodev.tmpfs.size = 25000000

-lxc.cap.keep = audit_control sys_nice wake_alarm setpcap setgid setuid sys_ptrace sys_admin wake_alarm block_suspend sys_time net_admin net_raw net_bind_service kill dac_override dac_read_search fsetid mknod syslog chown sys_resource fowner ipc_lock sys_chroot
+lxc.cap.keep = audit_control sys_nice setpcap setgid setuid sys_ptrace sys_admin block_suspend sys_time net_admin net_raw net_bind_service kill dac_override dac_read_search fsetid mknod syslog chown sys_resource fowner ipc_lock sys_chroot

 lxc.mount.auto = cgroup:ro
